Reference-Guided CUDA Pipeline Optimization Log
Date: 2026-09-17
Branch: agent/pytest-test-log

1. Background
Reference-guided A-line decorrelation pipeline processes:
- origin + s01-s50
- 51 volumes total
- each volume: 600 x 600 x 512
- GPU: NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 Ti, 16 GB
- backend: CuPy / CUDA
- chunk_rows: 600 (one complete volume per GPU chunk)

2. Main optimization steps

[Stage 1] Persistent GPU workspace
- Reused GPU buffers across origin + all 50 measurement volumes.
- Removed repeated allocation/free between volumes.
- GPU memory usage became stable instead of sawtooth.

[Stage 2] Full-frame processing
- Increased chunk_rows from conservative values to 600.
- One complete 600 x 600 x 512 volume is processed as one chunk.
- Reduced Python loop, CUDA scheduling and chunk-switch overhead.

[Stage 3] NCC / template subtraction optimization
- Fused NCC post-processing:
  amplitude threshold,
  best center selection,
  LS coefficient,
  matched decision.
- Replaced temporary shifted-template arrays with in-place CUDA subtraction.
- Fixed non-contiguous FFT view stride handling in fused CUDA kernel.

[Stage 4] Row-wise median optimization
Nsight Systems showed the main bottleneck was not explicit Python synchronize calls,
but internal synchronization/kernel launches generated by CuPy row-wise median operations.

Before row-median optimization:
- cudaStreamSynchronize:
  44,121 calls
  85.80 s
- cudaLaunchKernel:
  574,262 calls

A custom row-wise CUDA median kernel was introduced to replace cp.median(axis=1)
in the hot path.

After row-median optimization:
- cudaStreamSynchronize:
  57 calls
  19.12 s
- cudaLaunchKernel:
  2,246 calls

The custom median kernel keeps intermediate results on GPU and avoids the large
number of small reduction/sort kernels previously generated by CuPy.

3. Runtime results

Initial full-GPU baseline:
- Wall time: 3:16.22
- 196.22 s total
- ~3.85 s / volume

Sync-optimized version:
- Wall time: 2:58.17
- 178.17 s total
- ~3.49 s / volume

Median-optimized version:
- Wall time: 1:53.36
- 113.36 s total
- ~2.22 s / volume

Overall improvement:
- 196.22 s -> 113.36 s
- saved 82.86 s
- approximately 42.2% reduction in total wall time

