5. Important conclusion

High GPU utilization is not itself the optimization target.

Earlier versions showed higher CUDA utilization, but much of the activity came from:
- hundreds of thousands of small kernels
- frequent stream synchronization
- repeated reduction/median operations

The optimized version may show lower instantaneous CUDA utilization,
but completes the full workload substantially faster.

The main performance metric should therefore be end-to-end wall time,
while preserving CPU/GPU numerical agreement and automatic QC.

